[0.0, "o", "\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mYou're right. The case for space data centers as a way to get around the grid is mostly an  \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m↪\u001b[4;5H \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64margument about the US (and to some extent Europe). China mostly doesn't have that         \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m↪\u001b[5;5H \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mproblem, although it isn't completely free of power constraints.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m                          \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m                                                                                            \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:140:175:210m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m### \u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[38:2:140:175:210m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mWhy China looks different\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m              "]
[0.0, "o", "                                                 \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m                                                                                            \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:180:142:173m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m-\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m \u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m**Generation is growing much faster.**\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m In 2024 alone, China added 543 gigawatts of power  \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m↪\u001b[10;5H \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mcapacity—\u001b[10;15Hmore than the total capacity added by the U.S. \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4:3m\u001b[58:2::235:203:139m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64min\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m its entire history.            \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m↪\u001b[11;5H \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mProject"]
[0.0, "o", "ions put it at roughly 400 gigawatts of spare power capacity by 2030.              \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:180:142:173m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m-\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m \u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m**The state plans where data centers go.**\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m Under the \"East Data, West Compute\" (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4:3m\u001b[58:2::191:97:106m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m东数西算\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m) \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m↪\u001b[13;5H \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mprogram, China is shifting energy-intensive data centers to its resource-rich western     \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m↪\u001b[14;5H \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mregions (like Inner Mongolia), powered with surplus wind and solar. In the US, by         \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125"]
