[0.0, "o", ":46:52:64mSSO\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m) is a near-polar low Earth orbit whose plane turns slowly so \u001b[18;5H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mthat it \u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m**keeps the same angle to the Sun all year**\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m.                                   \u001b[19;5H                                                                                         \u001b[20;5H \u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m**The problem:**\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m The Earth moves around the Sun about 0.9856°\u001b[20;67H per day, which is 360°\u001b[20;90H a  \u001b[21;5H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64myear. A normal orbital plane stays roughly fixed relative to the stars. That means its  \u001b[22;5H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mangle to the Sun keeps changing over the year.                                       "]
[0.0, "o", "   \u001b[23;5H \u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m**The trick:**\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m The Earth bulges at the equator (the \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4:3m\u001b[58:2::191:97:106m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mJ2\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m effect), and that bulge slowly   \u001b[24;5H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:90:101:125m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mturns every tilted orbit's plane. The rate is roughly:                                  \u001b[H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:208:146:206m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m---\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m                                                                 \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:163:190:140m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m[claude-opus-5-5*[  \b\b🔧\u001b[1;92H  \b\b🌎\u001b[1;94H]]\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:126:129:136m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m   \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:136:192:208m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64mtopic\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:140:175:210m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38:2:205:206:207m\u001b[48:2:46:52:64m dawn-dusk sun-synchronous orbit                                                      \r\n\u001b(B\u001b["]
